[
  {
    "version": "1.0.114",
    "date": "2026-10-30",
    "sourceUrl": "https://github.com/brandonp2412/MarketMonk/compare/v1.0.113...v1.0.114",
    "changes": [
      "Candlestick (OHLC) view for stock charts, drawn with the same geometry as the line view. Tooltips and long-press scrubbing work on both.",
      "Desktop pages aligned: the profile and favorites pickers look the same on portfolio and holdings, page titles show the active profile, and chart padding matches the portfolio page.",
      "The portfolio header now summarizes positions and currencies. CSV actions moved into the profile picker, which also gained an initial profile picker.",
      "IBKR account values are estimated after the market closes and shown next to the official history. Trade history that failed to load is retried and cached, so holding details appear instantly.",
      "The chart search bar shows the selected symbol. Chart toggles moved into the mobile menu and settings, and the market-closed indicator is gone.",
      "Cached chart history opens without waiting for a sync, one-day charts include daily fund valuations, and tooltips stay responsive while switching periods.",
      "Favorites can be renamed from the action sheet and removed with a long-press bottom sheet, and the cached list shows while broker charts load.",
      "Interrupted network requests resume when the app comes back. Intraday broker requests pause when the connection fails.",
      "Flutter and dependency upgrade. External link buttons fixed on Android. The new-version notice can now be dismissed. Dead code and unused assets removed."
    ]
  },
  {
    "version": "1.0.113",
    "date": "2026-10-12",
    "sourceUrl": "https://github.com/brandonp2412/MarketMonk/compare/v1.0.112...v1.0.113",
    "changes": [
      "App data now lives in a single SQLite database. The old database is migrated automatically, backups and restore use the new store, and a new mm command-line tool can inspect the data.",
      "Intraday charts for stock prices from Yahoo and IBKR, plus intraday portfolio charts built from current holdings.",
      "Switching portfolio accounts is instant. IBKR chart data matches the broker's NAV, fed by a read-only LumiBot market data backend.",
      "Charts were rebuilt on the Drafter renderer. Desktop adds drag-to-zoom and right-click context menus, the rolling average moved into the chart controls, and cached charts draw immediately.",
      "New languages: Arabic, Bengali, Dutch, European Portuguese, Italian, Malay, Persian, Polish, Russian, Thai, Turkish, Ukrainian, Urdu, and Vietnamese.",
      "IBKR performance is read from the SQLite cache instead of the broker each time. Returns and realized P/L are reconciled, remote connections must use HTTPS, and trade history survives outages.",
      "Desktop portfolio and holdings were redesigned for compact windows. Tabs fade between pages, and a setting hides dollar amounts.",
      "New golden monk app icon. Releases now go out fortnightly. Portfolios can be shared or exported as CSV, holdings has an account switcher, and the app detects your local currency from the device region."
    ]
  },
